cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Concord in your research, please cite it as below, and cite every dataset you
  use with it (listed under references).
type: software
title: "Concord: a hardware-agnostic, read-only runtime and SDK for brain-computer interfaces"
abstract: >-
  Concord receives neural data from acquisition systems and recordings, labels every event
  with its provenance, runs decoders, and passes decoded commands only to applications an
  operator authorizes. Research software; validated in software and with protocol-level test
  sources only, not with acquisition hardware or participants.
authors:
  - name: "Concord contributors"
version: "0.3.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arnavhiteshpatel-cloud/concord"
keywords:
  - brain-computer interface
  - neural data
  - lab streaming layer
  - open ephys
  - neurodata without borders
  - decoding
